            <div xml:id="d493">

                <pb facs="0560" n="456" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg456"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4461: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai (Cunningham) to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-27T19:00:00+08:00">February 27, 1932—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 27—10:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>123. Continuing my daily report 113, February 26, 4 p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>There is little change to report. Japanese military have devoted most of
                        their time to reconnaissance and bombing work with planes. Some 40 planes
                        are said to be in the air at once each plane remaining 1 hour. They claim to
                        have destroyed approximately 10 Chinese planes at Hangchow in yesterday’s
                        raid. In addition to the raid at Hangchow they also machine-gunned a
                        supplemental field at Soochow. In their activities in and around the
                        Settlement the American marines report that 3 Japanese pursuit planes flew
                        over the Settlement outside billet number 12.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>A later report is to the effect that the Japanese have been bombing a fort
                        near Paoshan Village. The Japanese now report that they have completely
                        enveloped Kiangwan Village making it impossible for the Chinese defenders to
                        hold out much longer. They also claim to have straightened their lines
                        opposite Tazang Village.</item>
                </list>
                <p>Repeated to the Legation and Nanking. Copy to Minister.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
